# raBooks Enterprise Core Directive
- Integer Paisa Precision: Currency amounts must be stored and computed as signed 64-bit integer paise.
- Split Reconciliation Invariant: Delta between transaction total and allocated split rows must strictly be 0 paise.
- Dual-ID Decoupling: Canonical internal 'RB-TXN-XXXXXX' vs external UTR rail references.
- Spooler Sovereignty: Direct window.print() or detached Blob-URL window without forcing PDF file downloads.
- Corporate English: Strictly formal financial terminology.
- Non-Repudiation Audit: All mutations committed with audit_log entry.
